Z||000000||Ironhorse||06-22-2000||02:56 PM||||I was browsing the junkyard in my hometown and saw a 84-86(don't know year) pontiac 6000 seat in PERFECT condition.  If I change the track in my Fiero seat to the 6000 seat, will it work?  I ain't tellin ya how much it is or it'll be swap from under my nose  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">... I wanted to get the trans am seat but it was in terrible terrible condition.  Is this possible.. I've been looking everywhere on the net for a list of which seat will fit in a fiero, but no avail.  Thanks for any info||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||06-22-2000||04:40 PM||||6000s are basically Grand Ams, and People use  grand am seats, i think they'd fit. Measure the width if you're not sure.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-23-2000||10:38 AM||||My sister had a Pontiac 6000 SE.  It had a bench seat.  Seems to me it wouldn't work very well in a Fiero, but you're more than welcome to try.  I doubt the bench seat would be a chick magnet, though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||William Federle||06-23-2000||01:33 PM||||I don't know about that MM. It used to be a lot easier to get close to a girl on bench seats.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-23-2000||04:40 PM||||True, but since the bench seat would have to be high enough to clear the center console/fuel tank, clearance might be a problem.  Of course, if you're trying to get close to a girl, clearance might not be an issue. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
